-- title:
--   Relative fundamental theorem of Hopf modules for ideals
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring and $L$ a commutative $R$-Hopf algebra that is flat as an $R$-module, and let $S$ be a commutative $R$-algebra. Suppose given an $R$-algebra map $\delta : S \to S \otimes_R L$ satisfying, elementwise, the coassociativity identity $(\mathrm{assoc})\bigl((\delta \otimes \mathrm{id}_L)(\delta s)\bigr) = (\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \Delta)(\delta s)$ and the counit identity $(\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \varepsilon)(\delta s) = s \otimes 1$ in $S \otimes_R R$, so that $\delta$ makes $S$ an $L$-comodule algebra. Suppose further given a surjective $R$-algebra map $q : S \to L$ compatible with the coactions in the sense that $(q \otimes \mathrm{id}_L)(\delta s) = \Delta(q s)$ for all $s$, and an ideal $M \subseteq S$ such that the product ideal $(\ker q)\,M$ is zero and such that $\delta m$ lies in the ideal of $S \otimes_R L$ generated by the image of $M$ for every $m \in M$. Then two conclusions hold: first, $M$ is contained in the ideal of $S$ generated by the coinvariants lying in $M$, that is by $\{m \in M : \delta m = m \otimes 1\}$; second, every $m \in M$ can be written as $m = m_0 + r$ with $m_0 \in M$ satisfying $\delta m_0 = m_0 \otimes 1$ and $r$ in the product ideal $\ker(\varepsilon \circ q)\cdot M$, where $\varepsilon \circ q : S \to R$ is the composite of $q$ with the counit of $L$.
--
--   This is the fundamental theorem of Hopf modules in the relative form needed for a Hopf-module ideal inside a comodule algebra: the hypotheses make $M$ an $L$-Hopf module, with $L$ acting through $q$ because $\ker q$ annihilates $M$, and the conclusions express that $M$ is generated by its coinvariants and that $M^{\mathrm{co}} \to M/L^{+}M$ is surjective. It rests on [`HopfAlgebra.bijective_lift_coinvariants_and_bijective_mkQ_of_isHopfModule`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.bijective_lift_coinvariants_and_bijective_mkQ_of_isHopfModule) and is used in [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_sub_mem_and_firstOrder_invariant`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_sub_mem_and_firstOrder_invariant) to produce invariant elements of an ideal cutting out a finite infinitesimal subgroup of a formal module.
